    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 34 tests pass, including the new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD tier) and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) and `Cp11Tests` (household).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the GOLD membership tier rule following the codebase's existing derived-field pattern (the same shape as `namesakeCount`, `householdId`, etc.):\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field (`@Column(name = \"household_member_count\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column to the `owners` table.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added an `assignHouseholdMemberCount(owner)` step (run right after `assignHouseholdId`, since it depends on the assigned `householdId`). It counts existing owners sharing the same `householdId` and adds 1 for the owner being created, capturing the household size *after* this create.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 updated the `membershipTier` expression so GOLD takes priority: `householdMemberCount >= 3` \u2192 `GOLD`; otherwise the existing `SILVER` (namesakeCount 0 + email present) / `BRONZE` rules apply.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum and updated its description.\n\nBecause the count is computed at create time and persisted, the third household member is stored with `householdMemberCount = 3` and correctly reports `GOLD` on subsequent reads (`getOwner`), while the first two members retain their at-create counts (1 and 2) and keep the BRONZE/SILVER rules \u2014 faithful to the \"after this create\" wording in the spec.",
